        "id": 1483403
      },
      "writtenOn": "2026-09-15T22:32:28Z",
      "side": 1,
      "message": "The fan_table_to_rpm function in fan.c uses static variables (current_level, up_level_delay_count, etc.) to track state. These are not reset in test_fan_before, which means test cases within this suite can interfere with each other. \n\nYou should reset this state in test_fan_before. Since they are static in fan.c, you can trigger a reset by calling board_override_fan_control(0, temp) with chipset_in_state returning 0.",
